# Logo scroll baseline (approved checkpoint)

User-approved working state (Jul 9 2026). If logo scroll changes go wrong, revert scroll/morph logic to this baseline.

## Behavior

- Hero `.hero-title-image` visible at top; on scroll morph starts after `morphStart`
- **No `transform: scale()`** — logo shrinks via interpolated **width** (`heroW → headerW`) to preserve aspect ratio
- Floating `.scroll-logo` via `createPortal(document.body)`:
  - `position: fixed`, `left: 50%`, `transform: translate(-50%, -50%)`
  - `z-index: 103` — above header border line
  - Interpolated `top` from hero center to header center
  - White → gold crossfade on scroll-logo layers (linear `progress`)
- At `scrollY >= triggerEnd`: scroll-logo pinned in header slot, **clickable** (scroll to top)
- Header `.logo` stays invisible (`opacity: 0`) — only used for measuring `headerW` / `headerCenterVP`
- `morphRange = min(55vh, triggerEnd)`, linear progress

## Key files

- `client/src/App.tsx` — `measureHeroLogo`, `showScrollLogo` / `hideScrollLogo`, scroll `compute()`, portal `.scroll-logo`
- `client/src/App.css` — `.scroll-logo`, `.scroll-logo--pinned`, `.scroll-logo-inner`, `.scroll-logo-layer`, `.hero-title-layer` with `object-fit: contain`

## Measurement

- `naturalRef`: real image rect from first `img` in hero (fallback: `.hero-title` box), stores `centerAbs`
- Remeasure on load, resize, `provans-preloader-done`, timeout 3500ms
- `ProvansPreloader.jsx` dispatches `provans-preloader-done` on finish

## Do NOT reintroduce without user request

- `transform: scale()` on hero logo during morph (causes squished/distorted text)
- Moving morph on `.hero-title-image` with fixed + scale combo
- Showing header `.logo` with `logo--visible` as the pinned end state (use scroll-logo instead)
- Easing curves / handoff crossfade between hero and header elements

## Revert phrase

User can say: **«верни baseline логотипа»** — restore logic described above.
